WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:04.280
Marcus wants to reduce his insurance costs.

2
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.540
A producer says a new policy has identical benefits but hides

3
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:14.320
a shorter guarantee and a new surrender charge.

4
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:20.820
Misrepresentation means giving a false or misleading account of the policy.

5
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.020
Twisting involves misleading statements or incomplete comparisons intended

6
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:31.380
to induce a policy decision such as surrender, exchange

7
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.700
or lapse. Maryland's rule also covers inducing someone to retain a

8
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.140
policy through that conduct.

9
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.300
An honest, complete comparison can support a legitimate replacement.

10
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.940
A replacement is not automatically twisting; deception is the issue.

11
00:00:50.778 --> 00:00:55.878
Elena hears another agency repeat a false claim that

12
00:00:55.878 --> 00:00:57.858
an insurer is insolvent.

13
00:00:58.478 --> 00:01:03.938
Insurance defamation includes a false or maliciously critical statement

14
00:01:03.938 --> 00:01:09.218
about an insurer's financial condition that is calculated to injure

15
00:01:09.218 --> 00:01:14.538
the insurance business. False financial statements are also prohibited.

16
00:01:15.898 --> 00:01:21.198
Altering an insurer's records to deceive an examiner is not ordinary

17
00:01:21.198 --> 00:01:26.338
sales enthusiasm. Compare the facts: describing a

18
00:01:26.338 --> 00:01:31.718
real, documented policy limitation is different from inventing

19
00:01:31.718 --> 00:01:36.498
financial trouble. Verify information before sharing it,

20
00:01:37.158 --> 00:01:42.378
and explain the product without attacking a competitor through false claims.

21
00:01:43.188 --> 00:01:46.788
A producer offers to return part of a life premium personally

22
00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:48.308
if Aisha buys today.

23
00:01:49.388 --> 00:01:53.828
An off-contract premium rebate used to induce the sale can violate

24
00:01:53.828 --> 00:01:58.888
Maryland law. The state permits specified educational materials,

25
00:01:59.128 --> 00:02:03.988
promotional materials or merchandise costing no more than fifty dollars, but

26
00:02:03.988 --> 00:02:07.450
receipt cannot depend on buying insurance.

27
00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:11.328
A twenty-dollar promotional notebook available without a purchase

28
00:02:11.328 --> 00:02:15.608
condition is different from cash back only after a sale.

29
00:02:16.688 --> 00:02:18.248
Read both parts of the exception.

30
00:02:19.328 --> 00:02:23.668
A low dollar amount alone does not authorize a purchase-contingent reward.

31
00:02:24.438 --> 00:02:29.298
Unfair discrimination is not the same as every difference in premium.

32
00:02:30.138 --> 00:02:35.978
Maryland prohibits unfair differences among life-insurance applicants in

33
00:02:35.978 --> 00:02:38.978
the same class with equal expectation of life.

34
00:02:39.758 --> 00:02:45.178
Legitimate underwriting differences must still respect specific statutory

35
00:02:45.178 --> 00:02:49.578
protections. The life statute has particular rules for blindness,

36
00:02:50.418 --> 00:02:56.018
hearing impairment, specified harmless genetic traits and lawful travel.

37
00:02:57.038 --> 00:03:01.338
Do not replace these rules with stereotypes or a personal judgment

38
00:03:01.338 --> 00:03:06.898
about a community. Collect relevant facts, use lawful underwriting

39
00:03:06.898 --> 00:03:11.578
criteria and refer the decision to the insurer's authorized process.

40
00:03:12.578 --> 00:03:15.978
Respectful treatment applies to every applicant.

41
00:03:16.848 --> 00:03:20.128
Suppose a lender says Elena may obtain a loan only if

42
00:03:20.128 --> 00:03:23.028
she buys insurance through the lender's chosen producer.

43
00:03:23.848 --> 00:03:28.608
Maryland prohibits tying access to the listed goods, services or credit

44
00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:32.468
to buying insurance through a particular producer or insurer.

45
00:03:33.228 --> 00:03:36.368
Requiring suitable protection for a legitimate interest is a different

46
00:03:36.368 --> 00:03:38.188
question from forcing the seller.

47
00:03:38.948 --> 00:03:43.968
Another rule addresses concerted boycott, coercion or intimidation that

48
00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:46.568
unreasonably restrains the insurance business.

49
00:03:47.948 --> 00:03:50.988
Look for the actual pressure and the required relationship.

50
00:03:51.928 --> 00:03:55.168
A client must retain the free choice protected by the statute.

51
00:03:56.058 --> 00:04:00.378
A receptionist without a producer license can connect a customer with

52
00:04:00.378 --> 00:04:05.378
a licensed producer. That does not authorize the receptionist to recommend

53
00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:10.518
policy terms. Maryland's compensation statute permits certain payments

54
00:04:10.518 --> 00:04:15.798
to people who do not sell, solicit or negotiate, subject

55
00:04:15.798 --> 00:04:17.798
to its anti-inducement limits.

56
00:04:18.978 --> 00:04:22.858
Calling active sales work a referral does not make it lawful.

57
00:04:23.478 --> 00:04:26.018
The same care applies to documents.

58
00:04:26.858 --> 00:04:30.338
Do not ask a client to sign a blank application so

59
00:04:30.338 --> 00:04:32.158
answers can be invented later.

60
00:04:32.978 --> 00:04:37.938
Complete the facts accurately, obtain the required review and signatures,

61
00:04:38.838 --> 00:04:41.898
and use the insurer's approved correction process.
